NAME='Pluto'
COVER_SUB='What a generation transforms, from 12 to 30 years in each sign.'
T=[
('1823–51','Pluto in Aries, its sign of exaltation in the traditional view and Mars’s house, shows itself with unprecedented violence. The passage of the planet through Aries influenced and produced important metamorphoses, with revolutions and the birth of new nations. It is the will to rebirth by force. Karmic reading: a generation forced to start over. The shadow is violence and the urge to destroy what resists. The lesson: transformation without cruelty.'),
('1853–84','In Taurus Pluto loses much of its personality and becomes a mysterious worker. The sign forces it to act, create, generate mysterious machines and even discover ingenious inventions. Pluto in Taurus scorns violence in favour of discovery. Industry, railways, banks and the control of resources transform society. Karmic reading: a generation that rebuilt the relationship with the earth and with wealth. The shadow is greed and possession. The lesson: what you own can own you.'),
('1884–1914','Pluto in Gemini seems to mark a pause, giving the impression of secretly preparing one of its left-handed blows. In the double sign of Gemini it plays a role of twofold metamorphosis, in communication, transport, press, telephone, radio and the exchange of ideas. A generation of new voices. Karmic reading: a generation transforming how the world talks to itself. The shadow is manipulation by information. The lesson: words create worlds.'),
('1914–39','In the feminine, passive and dreamy sign of Cancer, Pluto lets itself be dragged into excess. In the Moon’s house and in Jupiter’s sign of exaltation it influences the family and social relations: attachment to roots, nation, homeland, and crises of belonging. A generation marked by war, migration and the shaking of the home. Karmic reading: a generation healing the collective family. The shadow is nationalism and fear. The lesson: safety is shared.'),
('1939–58','Pluto in Leo tends to impose itself in a mysterious and dramatic way. It acts as a catalyst and works in depth to produce showy outward metamorphoses. In the Sun’s house it signals the power of leaders and the centrality of the individual. This generation witnessed dictators, atomic energy and the rise of the self. Karmic reading: a generation learning the cost of power. The shadow is pride and control. The lesson: true power does not need to be feared.'),
('1958–72','The transit of Pluto in Virgo influences above all work and money; interest is the dominant element. In this period electronics and information technology took hold, starting the era of computers. This generation changed health, work and efficiency, and questioned the system of service. Karmic reading: a generation purifying daily life. The shadow is excessive control and obsession with detail. The lesson: a system must serve people.'),
('1972–84','In its fall in Libra, Pluto does not lose its transforming influence. With dissonant planetary aspects it signals unstable and upsetting situations, yet it holds up well. Marriage, divorce, law, partnership and the balance between the sexes are transformed. Karmic reading: a generation learning that relationship is a mirror. The shadow is power games in couples. The lesson: equality is a daily practice.'),
('1984–95','In its own house, Pluto plays a preponderant role. This passage produced great transformations in social, economic and family life. Worldwide there was the triumph of the atomic era, the unstoppable spread of drugs and prostitution, but also awareness of ecological and healing movements. Karmic reading: a generation facing the shadow collectively. The shadow is obsession and the abuse of power. The lesson: what you face, you can change.'),
('1995–2008','In Jupiter’s benefic house, Pluto influences relations with foreigners and with abroad, scientific research, esoteric doctrines and spirituality. It also marks travel, adventures and mass emigration, along with exploration and discovery. It signals an important spiritual metamorphosis. Beliefs, globalisation and religion are transformed. Karmic reading: a generation that expanded the world and now questions its meaning. The shadow is fanaticism. The lesson: a truth imposed on others becomes a weapon.'),
('2008–24','In methodical, rational and constructive Capricorn, Pluto tends to concentrate on spiritual relations at world level and on transforming consciences, directing them toward new horizons. Governments, finance and institutions are shaken from the foundation, and old structures have to justify themselves. Karmic reading: a generation dismantling inherited authority. The shadow is cynicism and fear of collapse. The lesson: rebuild on honesty.'),
('2024–44','In Aquarius, the anticonformist sign and the house of explosive Uranus, Pluto’s work of demolition and reconstruction seems favoured. It signals revolutionary momentum and great collective changes: technology, artificial intelligence, networks, who owns knowledge. Karmic reading: a generation that decides what humanity does with its power. The shadow is cold systems and control of the many by the few. The lesson: progress that leaves people behind is not progress.'),
('2044–68','In Pisces, the subtle and intriguing energy of the sign joins the slow metamorphosis of Pluto, marking deep transformations at personal and social level. It dissolves old beliefs, with a new spirituality, healing and compassion, and the redefinition of the invisible. Karmic reading: a generation at the end of a very long cycle, dissolving what is no longer needed. The shadow is escapism and confusion. The lesson: letting go is also creation.'),
]
